post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
Yoru is at /usr/bin/yoru. Starting him at login, the key that hides him and
the key that swaps the character are your Hyprland config, which a package
does not write. Three lines:

  ~/.config/hypr/autostart.lua
    o.launch_on_start("/usr/bin/yoru")

  ~/.config/hypr/bindings.lua
    o.bind("SUPER + CTRL + Y", "Toggle Yoru", "pkill -USR1 -f 'python3 /usr/bin/yoru( |$)'")
    o.bind("SUPER + CTRL + SHIFT + Y", "Swap Yoru", "pkill -USR2 -f 'python3 /usr/bin/yoru( |$)'")

Autostart takes effect at your next login; until then:  yoru &
Try the knobs first:  yoru --interval 20 --roam 20 --idle 0
MSG
}

# Super + Ctrl + Shift + Y arrived in 1.1.0, and post_install does not run on
# an upgrade -- so anyone who installed before it would never be told the key
# exists, which for a keybinding is the same as it not existing. Told once, to
# the people it is new to.
post_upgrade() {
  if [ -n "$2" ] && [ "$(vercmp "$2" 1.1.0)" -lt 0 ]; then
    cat <<'MSG'
New in 1.1.0: a second character, and a key to swap him in. One more line in
~/.config/hypr/bindings.lua, then hyprctl reload:

    o.bind("SUPER + CTRL + SHIFT + Y", "Swap Yoru", "pkill -USR2 -f 'python3 /usr/bin/yoru( |$)'")

Or start as him with:  yoru --sprite dane
MSG
  fi
}
